.Dd $Mdocdate: November 18 2026 $
.Dt IMAPIDLECTL 1
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm imapidlectl
.Nd show and set imapidle memory
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm imapidlectl
.Op Fl s Ar path
.Op Ar name ...
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
asks the running
.Sy imapidle(1)
for the values it holds in memory.
The default socket is
.Pa ~/var/run/imapidle.sock .
.Fl s
names another socket.
.Pp
With no
.Ar name ,
every node is printed as
.Ar name Ns = Ns Ar value .
A
.Ar name
prints that node and every node under it.
.Ar name Ns = Ns Ar value
sets a writable node and prints the result.
.Pp
A component that contains a dot is written with the dot doubled,
so a mailbox
.Ql INBOX.Sent
is
.Ql INBOX..Sent .
.Pp
.Ar shutdown=1
asks the daemon to exit the way
.Dv SIGTERM
does.
It does not create a shutdown file, so the next start is not held.
.Ar pause=1
pauses
.Sy mbsync
the way a pause file does.
.Ar pause=0
clears a pause that was set this way.
A pause file is left in place and still pauses.
.Ar account.name.folder.box.resync
sets how long that watched folder may go since its last sync.
The value is whole seconds, at least 60.
The default is 43200.
A dot inside the mailbox name is still doubled.
A reload reads the value from the configuration again.
.Pp
.Ar account.name.folder.box.last_sync
is when that folder's
.Sy mbsync
last started, in whole seconds since the epoch.
Zero means this process has not started one.
.Ar last_sync_clock
is that time in the local zone, as
.Ql YYYYMMDD HH:MM:SS.uuuuuu .
.Ar next_sync
is
.Ar last_sync
plus the folder's resync time, and
.Ar next_sync_clock
is that instant in the same form.
.Ar late
is how many whole seconds that instant is past, or 0 while
it is still ahead.
.Ar priority
and
.Ar debounce
are the folder's priority and its minimum gap, in seconds.
The same last instant is also
.Ar schedule.channel.folder.box.last
and
.Ar last_clock ,
using the
.Sy mbsync
channel name.
.Ar pending
is 1 while an arrival is waiting out that gap.
.Ar schedule.channel.deadline
is the channel's combine time, in whole seconds since the
epoch, and
.Ar deadline_clock
is that instant.
.Ar late
on the channel is how many seconds that deadline is past.
.Ar busy
is 1 while
.Sy mbsync
is already running for the channel.
.Ar schedule.channel.folder.box.queued
is 1 while the folder sits in that combine window.
A write of these nodes is refused.
.Ar account.name.hyperdelete
is 1 to sync a removal, or 0 to leave it until the next arrival
or that folder's resync time.
A reload reads this value from the configuration again.
.Ar account.name.next_try
is when that account logs in again, as seconds since the epoch.
Zero tries on the next loop.
Three authentication failures in a row set this one week ahead.
The write clears that hold.
.Ar account.name.disabled
is 0 or 1.
The write is remembered until the next start or reload.
The configuration file is not rewritten, and the file is applied
again at start and at reload.
.Ar disabled=1
drops that account's connections and does not set a future login.
.Ar disabled=0
clears the pause, the connect backoff, and a pending login hold,
including an authentication week.
.Ar limit.server.port.user.cap
is how many sessions this process may hold for that server,
port, and user.
The value is a whole number.
Zero is allowed.
.Ar limit.server.port.user.probe
is when one extra session may be tried, in seconds since
the epoch.
Zero tries on the next login.
A dot inside the server or the user is doubled.
Both values are kept in
.Pa ~/.local/imapidle/conn-limit
and a reload leaves them in place.
A write this process does not apply is an error.
.Pp
.Ar sched.now
and
.Ar sched.now_clock
are the time of this listing.
.Ar sched.pump_depth
counts scheduler passes open in this process.
A listing answered from inside a pass shows 1.
.Ar sched.hot_pump
is 1 while a pass already in progress is starting a due
watched-folder sync.
.Ar sched.slots_hot
and
.Ar sched.slots_cold
are the free
.Sy mbsync
slots for watched folders and for tracked or pulse folders.
.Ar sched.loop_wait
is the seconds the main loop would sleep on its next wait.
.Ar sched.batches
is how many channels have a combine window open.
.Ar sched.pending
is how many folders are waiting on a gap or a window.
.Ar account.name.next_try_clock
is listed when
.Ar next_try
is in the future, in the same local form as
.Ar last_sync_clock .
.Ar account.name.limit_blocked
is 1 while the learned connection cap is holding a new login.
.Ar pulse.name.channel.account.last
is when that pulse channel last finished a sweep, in whole
seconds since the epoch.
.Ar conn.name.what.idling
is 1 while that connection is inside
.Cm IDLE .
A pulse connection uses
.Cm PULSE
for
.Ar what .
.Ar conn.name.what.last_success
is when that connection last finished a housekeeping pass,
in whole seconds since the epoch.
A write of any of these is refused.
.Pp
The reply is one node per line.
An unknown name or a rejected write is an error on standard error,
and
.Nm
exits 1.
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Pa ~/var/run/imapidle.sock
The default socket.
Mode 0600.
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Ex -std imapidlectl
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Sy imapidle(1) ,
.Sy imapidle.conf(5)
